{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1509681-compact-bureau-of-unexplained-phenomena","id":1509681,"title":"Compact: Bureau of Unexplained Phenomena","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-25T20:32:23-07:00","id":1509681,"title":"Compact: Bureau of Unexplained Phenomena","content":"The Bureau of Unexplained Phenomena (BUP) is a government agency tasked with investigating reports of strange and unusual occurrences across the country. The agency was established in the late 1940s as the Cold War began and rumors of Soviet espionage and secret weapon projects were rampant. In response, the US government formed the BUP to investigate any strange phenomena that could potentially pose a threat to national security.<br /> <br /> However, as the years went by, the BUP's reputation began to suffer. Most of the cases the agents investigated turned out to be hoaxes, pranks, or misunderstandings, and the agency became known as a joke organization. Despite this, the BUP continued to operate, sending its agents out to investigate reports of UFO sightings, mysterious creatures, and other unexplained phenomena.<br /> <br /> They were rescued from being completely defunded in the late 1950s, when a Senior Agent by the name of Kent Mansley was sent to investigate reports of an alien robot in Rockwell, Maine. The Iron Giant Incident, as it is called in hushed whispers, resulted in a stunning turnaround of the bureau's fortunes and Mansley's promotion to Director. They finally had enough resources to field expert teams of investigators, backed by a hardnosed science team, and well-integrated into the rest of the bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> They never shed their reputations as jokes, but they don't try to anymore. It's easier to stick your nose into some spooky thing's business when they ignore you and as an acknowledged part of the federal government's intelligence and security apparatus, they can be surprisingly well-informed. After a few disasters in the field, the BUP has almost completely given up on combat. When necessary they prefer to hand anything dangerous off to more specialized and combat-focused organizations like Task Force Valkyrie or the Malleus Maleficarum. Rumors that they work with even stranger partners than those are not to be discussed, but they share enough of their investigation notes not to sour their relationships with the people they try to send into danger. Aside from keeping their own agents alive, this aversion to violence helps them maintain their harmless facade.<br /> <br /> There are three main divisions of the organization Arlington, Detroit, and Rockwell. They got their names from proposed locations for their individual headquarters despite the fact they never got separate headquarters and are all based in a single building in Gaithersburg, Maryland. Arlington focuses on maintaining good relations with other organizations split about half-and-half between other government organizations that might have leads for them and more secretive organizations relevant to the vigil. Detroit focuses on lab work to study samples that are recovered from the field. They are extremely suspicious of the paranormal and that limits what they can do, but they still manage to reverse-engineer enough technology to earn their paychecks. Rockwell which contains all of the field agents. Many of these are recruited from other federal agencies and would still fit in with their old coworkers, but a large and weird minority were recruited directly to BUP. These tend to be the strangest people in the organization, but they haven't finished training until they can at least act normal.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Benefits of membership in the Bureau of Unexplained Phenomena</u><br /> <br /> \u2022 You have enough training to do your job and that means keeping a low profile. Take a free Subterfuge specialty in &quot;Feigning normalcy.&quot;<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain 3 free dots to distribute between Allies and Contacts representing organizations that you may call on to support your vigil.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The only person with this much status is the Director. What benefits a player character who manages to earn this in-story gets is unknown, but the Storyteller is advised to pick something equivalent to a 3-dot merit.\u200b<br /> <br /> <i>AN: This is mostly intended as a writing exercise. To take an agency mentioned in one or two lines of the Iron Giant and see how they might actually fit in HtV. They are distinguished from Task Force Valkyrie by being largely non-combatants and from VASCU by dealing with every kind of weirdness and not just Slashers.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}